<!-- EvoX Settings integration: launch DualMessenger from Settings search + dashboard.
Copy ONE file into Settings, no Java duplication (Settings just fires intent).

1) In packages/apps/Settings/res/xml/evolution_dashboard.xml (or equivalent cnb file) add:

    <Preference
        android:key="dual_messenger"
        android:title="@string/dual_messenger_title"
        android:summary="@string/dual_messenger_summary"
        android:icon="@drawable/ic_dual_messenger"
        android:fragment="" >
        <intent android:action="com.clonepilot.app.OPEN" />
    </Preference>

2) In packages/apps/Settings/res/values/evolution_strings.xml add:

    <string name="dual_messenger_title">Dual Messenger</string>
    <string name="dual_messenger_summary">نسخة ثانية ومتعددة بنمط سامسونج</string>

3) Copy ic_dual_messenger.xml from this folder to
   packages/apps/Settings/res/drawable/ic_dual_messenger.xml

4) For Settings search indexing (optional, cnb uses SearchIndexProvider):
   Add to your dashboard fragment's SEARCH_INDEX_DATA_PROVIDER the key "dual_messenger".
   No controller needed because we use <intent>, not fragment.

Why intent and not fragment? Keeps ClonePilot standalone + reachable from Settings.
Both requirements (مستقلة + مدمجة) are satisfied with zero code duplication.
-->
<PreferenceScreen xmlns:android="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res/android">
    <!-- snippet only, see instructions above -->
</PreferenceScreen>
